      "writtenOn": "2024-01-04T11:56:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This are harcoded in the host command definition so they\u0027ll never change, I even added a test to make sure they don\u0027t change ever. I could define them as offset from absent but don\u0027t quite see the point to be honest, this is the simplest I could come up with.\n\nBTW ideally they\u0027d only be defined once and I could get rid of the host command defines, but first, that\u0027s an enum and it\u0027s not quite automatic to kill the enum, and second I\u0027d have to include a zephyr specific file from a common header, which does not sound quite right, so this is where I landed. Should be good enough since there\u0027s a test for coherency.",
